IMPORTANT NOTICE:
The dataset "pcsaft_novel_predictions_v1.csv" contains MODEL-GENERATED PREDICTIONS,
not experimental measurements. All PC-SAFT parameters (m, σ, ε/k) are predicted by
machine learning models trained on experimental data from literature sources.

Do not use this dataset for:
  - Direct engineering design or safety calculations
  - Regulatory compliance or environmental risk assessment
  - Physical property databases (represent as predictions, not experimental data)
  - Training new PC-SAFT prediction models (to avoid circular dependencies)

See data/DATASHEET.md for full documentation of composition, limitations, and uses.

Training Data Attribution:
The models that generated this predictive library were trained on experimental data from:
  - Esper et al. (2017), "PCP-SAFT Parameters", Figshare Collection 6821654
  - Felton et al. (2024), "ML-SAFT: Machine Learning Framework", GitHub repository
  - Thol et al. (SPT-PCSAFT database), Dortmund Data Bank

Users of this dataset must cite both this predictive library AND the original training
data sources listed in CITATION.cff.
